/-!
# Flat over regular with regular closed fibre is regular

All rings are commutative with unit; we work with local Noetherian rings and local ring
homomorphisms.

## Main result

Let `φ : R → S` be a local homomorphism of local Noetherian rings. If `R` is regular, the
closed fibre `S / m_R S` is regular, and `φ` is flat, then `S` is regular.

## Notation

A local ring is a commutative ring `R` with a unique maximal ideal `m_R`, recorded as
`IsLocalRing R` with `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`. A ring homomorphism `φ : R → S` between
local rings is local when `φ(m_R) ⊆ m_S`, equivalently `φ⁻¹(m_S) = m_R`, which is
`IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)`. A Noetherian local ring `(R, m_R)` is regular when its
Krull dimension equals the minimal number of generators of `m_R`; `IsRegularLocalRing R`
bundles `IsLocalRing` and `IsNoetherian R R` with the defining equality
`spanFinrank (maximalIdeal R) = ringKrullDim R`. Flatness of `R → S` is `Module.Flat R S`.

The closed fibre of a local homomorphism `R → S` is the quotient `S / m_R S`, where
`m_R S = (maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S)`. Locality gives `m_R S ≤ m_S`, so the
closed fibre is again a Noetherian local ring, with maximal ideal the image of `m_S`.

## Proof outline

Write `m_R`, `m_S` for the maximal ideals and `F = S / m_R S` for the closed fibre. For a
Noetherian local ring the embedding dimension is `Submodule.spanFinrank (maximalIdeal ·)`
and the dimension is `ringKrullDim ·`, and `IsRegularLocalRing` is by definition the
equality of the two. The argument combines two facts about a flat local homomorphism of
Noetherian local rings,

* (A) the dimension formula `dim S = dim R + dim F`, and
* (B) subadditivity of embedding dimension, `embdim S ≤ embdim R + embdim F`,

with two general facts about Noetherian local rings: (C) regular is equivalent to
`embdim = dim`, and (D) `dim ≤ embdim`. Chaining them,

`embdim S ≤ embdim R + embdim F = dim R + dim F = dim S ≤ embdim S`,

forces `embdim S = dim S`, i.e. `S` is regular.
-/

@[expose] public section

/-- The closed fibre `S / m_R S` of a local homomorphism `R → S`, i.e. the
quotient of `S` by the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `R`. -/
@[ega "0 19.7.1",
  ega "I 3.7.2" "special case",
  ega "IV 12.1.1.4" "special case",
  ega "IV 6.1.3",
  sga "1 III 1.7",
  sga "3 XXVI 7.15" "special case"]
abbrev ClosedFibre (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] : Type _ :=
  S ⧸ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S)

/-- For a local homomorphism `R → S`, the ideal `m_R S` is contained in the maximal
ideal `m_S`, hence is a proper ideal. -/
@[ega "0 1.0.7" "local implies φ(m)⊆n"]
theorem ClosedFibre.mapMaximalIdeal_le (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] :
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S) ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S :=
  IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_le (algebraMap R S)

/-- The closed fibre of a local homomorphism of local rings is a local ring. -/
@[ega "0 6.6.2" "partial"]
instance ClosedFibre.instIsLocalRing (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] :
    IsLocalRing (ClosedFibre R S) := by
  have hne : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S) ≠ ⊤ :=
    ne_top_of_le_ne_top (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal S).ne_top
      (ClosedFibre.mapMaximalIdeal_le R S)
  have : Nontrivial (ClosedFibre R S) := Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
  exact IsLocalRing.of_surjective'
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S)))
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

open IsLocalRing Submodule

/-- The maximal ideal of the closed fibre is the image of the maximal ideal of `S`. -/
private theorem ClosedFibre.maximalIdeal_eq_map (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] :
    maximalIdeal (ClosedFibre R S) =
      (maximalIdeal S).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk ((maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S))) :=
  (map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective).symm

/-- **(A) Dimension formula for a flat local homomorphism** (Stacks 00ON).
For a flat local homomorphism `R → S` of Noetherian local rings, the Krull
dimension of `S` is the sum of the dimension of `R` and the dimension of the
closed fibre `F = S / m_R S`:
`dim S = dim R + dim F`.

Both `R` and `S` are local Noetherian, so
`dim R = height m_R` and `dim S = height m_S`
(`maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim`).  The map is flat, hence satisfies
going-down (`Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat`), and `m_S` lies over `m_R`
(`IsLocalHom`: the contraction of `m_S` is `m_R`).  The Stacks 00ON dimension
formula `Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown` then gives
`height m_S = height m_R + height (m_S · in the fibre)`,
where the fibre ideal is `(m_S).map (Quotient.mk (m_R.map (algebraMap R S)))`,
which is exactly the maximal ideal of `F = ClosedFibre R S`.  Since `F` is local
Noetherian, `height (m_F) = dim F`.  Casting the `ℕ∞`-valued height identity into
`WithBot ℕ∞` yields the stated equality of Krull dimensions. -/
@[ega "IV 21.10.1" "partial",
  ega "IV 6.1.1" "Flat case of (6.1.1.1)",
  ega "IV 6.1.2",
  ega "IV 6.1.3" "special case"]
theorem ringKrullDim_eq_add_ringKrullDim_closedFibre (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing S] [IsNoetherianRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)]
    (hflat : Module.Flat R S) :
    ringKrullDim S = ringKrullDim R + ringKrullDim (ClosedFibre R S) := by
  have : Algebra.HasGoingDown R S := Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat
  have hlo : (maximalIdeal S).LiesOver (maximalIdeal R) :=
    Ideal.LiesOver.mk (maximalIdeal_comap (algebraMap R S)).symm
  have hkey := Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown
    (maximalIdeal R) (maximalIdeal S)
  rw [← ClosedFibre.maximalIdeal_eq_map] at hkey
  rw [← maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim (R := S),
    ← maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim (R := R),
    ← maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim (R := ClosedFibre R S), hkey]
  push_cast
  rfl

/-- For submodules `K ≤ p`, the span rank of `p` is at most the span rank of `K` plus the span
rank of the image of `p` in `M ⧸ K`. -/
private theorem Submodule.spanRank_le_spanRank_add_spanRank_map_mkQ {A M : Type*} [Ring A]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] {p K : Submodule A M} (h : K ≤ p) :
    p.spanRank ≤ K.spanRank + (p.map K.mkQ).spanRank := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha_card, ha_span⟩ := Submodule.exists_span_set_card_eq_spanRank K
  obtain ⟨b, hb_card, hb_span⟩ := Submodule.exists_span_set_card_eq_spanRank (p.map K.mkQ)
  have hb : ∀ y ∈ b, y ∈ p.map K.mkQ := fun y hy => by
    rw [← hb_span]
    exact Submodule.subset_span hy
  choose! g hgp hgK using fun y hy => Submodule.mem_map.mp (hb y hy)
  set c : Set M := a ∪ (g '' b) with hc
  have hsub : g '' b ⊆ (p : Set M) := by
    rintro x ⟨y, hyb, rfl⟩
    exact hgp y hyb
  have himg : K.mkQ '' (g '' b) = b := by
    ext y
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨z, ⟨w, hwb, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      rw [hgK w hwb]
      exact hwb
    · intro hyb
      exact ⟨g y, ⟨y, hyb, rfl⟩, hgK y hyb⟩
  have hspan : Submodule.span A c = p := by
    apply le_antisymm
    · rw [hc, Submodule.span_union, sup_le_iff]
      exact ⟨by rw [ha_span]; exact h, by rw [Submodule.span_le]; exact hsub⟩
    · intro x hx
      have hmkx : K.mkQ x ∈ Submodule.map K.mkQ (Submodule.span A (g '' b)) := by
        rw [Submodule.map_span, himg, hb_span]
        exact Submodule.mem_map_of_mem hx
      obtain ⟨z, hz, hzx⟩ := hmkx
      have hxz : x - z ∈ K := by
        have hzero : K.mkQ (x - z) = 0 := by rw [map_sub, hzx, sub_self]
        rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at hzero
        exact hzero
      have hz' : z ∈ Submodule.span A c :=
        Submodule.span_mono (by rw [hc]; exact Set.subset_union_right) hz
      have hxz' : x - z ∈ Submodule.span A c := by
        have hmem : x - z ∈ Submodule.span A a := by rw [ha_span]; exact hxz
        exact Submodule.span_mono (by rw [hc]; exact Set.subset_union_left) hmem
      simpa using Submodule.add_mem _ hxz' hz'
  calc p.spanRank = (Submodule.span A c).spanRank := by rw [hspan]
    _ ≤ Cardinal.mk c := Submodule.spanRank_span_le_card c
    _ ≤ Cardinal.mk a + Cardinal.mk (g '' b) := Cardinal.mk_union_le a (g '' b)
    _ ≤ Cardinal.mk a + Cardinal.mk b := by gcongr; exact Cardinal.mk_image_le
    _ = K.spanRank + (p.map K.mkQ).spanRank := by rw [ha_card, hb_card]

/-- **(B) Embedding-dimension subadditivity** for a flat local homomorphism.
For a local homomorphism `R → S` of Noetherian local rings with closed fibre
`F = S / m_R S`, the minimal number of generators of `m_S` is at most the sum
of those of `m_R` and of `m_F`:
`spanFinrank m_S ≤ spanFinrank m_R + spanFinrank m_F`.

Let `k = S / m_S` be the residue field of `S`; it is also the
residue field of the fibre `F`.  The cotangent space `m_S / m_S^2` is a finite
dimensional `k`-vector space and `spanFinrank m_S = dim_k (m_S / m_S^2)` (by
Nakayama, the minimal number of generators of `m_S` equals the `k`-dimension of
its cotangent space).  Because the map is local, `m_R S ⊆ m_S`
(`ClosedFibre.mapMaximalIdeal_le`), so the images of `φ(m_R)` span a subspace
`V ⊆ m_S / m_S^2` of dimension at most `spanFinrank m_R` (the `φ(x_i)` for a
minimal generating set `x_i` of `m_R` span `V`).  The quotient
`(m_S / m_S^2) / V` is naturally `m_F / m_F^2`, the cotangent space of the fibre
`F = S / m_R S` (its maximal ideal is `m_S / m_R S`, so its cotangent space is
the cokernel of `V → m_S/m_S^2`).  Hence
`dim_k (m_S/m_S^2) = dim_k V + dim_k (m_F/m_F^2) ≤ spanFinrank m_R + spanFinrank m_F`.
Concretely: take minimal generating sets of `m_R` (size `spanFinrank m_R`) and
of `m_F` (size `spanFinrank m_F`); lifting the latter to `S` and adjoining the
images `φ(x_i)` produces a generating set of `m_S` of size at most the sum,
whence `spanFinrank m_S` (the *minimal* size) is at most the sum. -/
theorem spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le_add_spanFinrank_closedFibre (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing
  S]
    [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing S] [IsNoetherianRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] :
    spanFinrank (maximalIdeal S)
      ≤ spanFinrank (maximalIdeal R) + spanFinrank (maximalIdeal (ClosedFibre R S)) := by
  -- Set up the ideal `I = m_R · S` and the quotient `F = S / I = ClosedFibre R S`.
  set I : Ideal S := (maximalIdeal R).map (algebraMap R S) with hI
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  -- `K = I ≤ p = m_S`.
  have hIle : I ≤ maximalIdeal S := ClosedFibre.mapMaximalIdeal_le R S
  -- Apply the general lemma (over `S`, so a single-universe cardinal inequality).
  have hmain := Submodule.spanRank_le_spanRank_add_spanRank_map_mkQ hIle
  -- Identify `(m_S).map I.mkQ` (over `S`) with `(maximalIdeal F).restrictScalars S`.
  have hbridge : ((maximalIdeal (ClosedFibre R S)).restrictScalars S)
      = Submodule.map I.mkQ (maximalIdeal S) := by
    rw [ClosedFibre.maximalIdeal_eq_map]
    ext x
    simp only [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, Submodule.mem_map]
    rw [Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective _ hsurj]
    rfl
  -- The restriction of scalars preserves `spanRank` since `S → F` is surjective.
  have hsurjAlg : Function.Surjective (algebraMap S (ClosedFibre R S)) := hsurj
  have hrest : (Submodule.map I.mkQ (maximalIdeal S)).spanRank
      = (maximalIdeal (ClosedFibre R S)).spanRank := by
    rw [← hbridge, Submodule.spanRank_restrictScalars_eq hsurjAlg]
  -- Finiteness (Noetherian ⇒ FG ⇒ spanRank finite) to pass to `toNat`.
  have hfinI : I.spanRank < Cardinal.aleph0 :=
    Submodule.spanRank_finite_iff_fg.mpr (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  have hfinM : (Submodule.map I.mkQ (maximalIdeal S)).spanRank < Cardinal.aleph0 := by
    rw [hrest]
    exact Submodule.spanRank_finite_iff_fg.mpr (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  -- Convert the cardinal inequality `hmain` to a `ℕ` inequality on `spanFinrank`.
  have hSF : (maximalIdeal S).spanFinrank
      ≤ I.spanFinrank + (Submodule.map I.mkQ (maximalIdeal S)).spanFinrank := by
    have hle := Cardinal.toNat_le_toNat hmain (Cardinal.add_lt_aleph0 hfinI hfinM)
    rwa [Cardinal.toNat_add hfinI hfinM] at hle
  -- Subadditivity of `spanFinrank` (in `ℕ`) under a ring-hom image: for an ideal
  -- `q` of a Noetherian ring `A`, the image `Ideal.map f q` is generated by the
  -- images of a minimal generating set of `q`, so its `spanFinrank` is no larger.
  -- `spanFinrank I ≤ spanFinrank m_R` and the fibre identification.
  have hIfin : I.spanFinrank ≤ (maximalIdeal R).spanFinrank :=
    Ideal.spanFinrank_map_le_of_fg (algebraMap R S) (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  have hFfin : (Submodule.map I.mkQ (maximalIdeal S)).spanFinrank
      = (maximalIdeal (ClosedFibre R S)).spanFinrank := by
    rw [Submodule.spanFinrank, Submodule.spanFinrank, hrest]
  -- Chain the `ℕ` inequalities.
  omega

/-- Let `φ : R → S` be a local homomorphism of local
Noetherian rings such that:
1. `R` is regular,
2. the closed fibre `S / m_R S` is regular, and
3. `φ : R → S` is flat.
Then `S` is regular. -/
@[stacks 031E,
  ega "IV 6.5.2" "(ii), local case",
  sga "1 I 9.1" "A regular ⇒ B regular",
  ega "IV 7.5.1.1" "special case"]
theorem isRegularLocalRing_of_flat_of_closedFibre (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing S] [IsNoetherianRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)]
    (hR : IsRegularLocalRing R)
    (hfibre : IsRegularLocalRing (ClosedFibre R S))
    (hflat : Module.Flat R S) :
    IsRegularLocalRing S := by
  -- (D) the reverse Krull bound: dim S ≤ embdim S.
  -- antisymmetry ⇒ embdim S = dim S ⇒ (C) ⇒ S regular.
  refine { spanFinrank_maximalIdeal := le_antisymm ?_ (ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal S) }
  -- (A) dimension formula, and (C) regular ⇒ embdim = dim, for R and for the fibre F.
  rw [ringKrullDim_eq_add_ringKrullDim_closedFibre R S hflat, ← hR.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal,
    ← hfibre.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal]
  -- (B) embdim subadditivity. Combine: embdim S ≤ embdim R + embdim F = dim R + dim F = dim S.
  exact_mod_cast spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le_add_spanFinrank_closedFibre R S

/-!
# Regularity descends along a flat local homomorphism

Let `R → S` be a local homomorphism of local Noetherian rings which is flat, and let `S` be
regular. Then `R` is regular. This is Stacks 00OF.

The proof is the source's. Write `𝔪 ⊂ R` for the maximal ideal and `κ = R/𝔪` for the residue
field, and let `d = dim S`. Resolve `κ` by finite free `R`-modules; because `R → S` is flat the
base change of that resolution to `S` stays exact, and because the global dimension of `S` is `d`
(Proposition 00O7) the `d`-th syzygy becomes a finite projective `S`-module. By Lemma 00O1 the
`d`-th syzygy is then already finite projective over `R`, so `κ` has projective dimension at most
`d` and `R` is regular by Proposition 00OC.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RegularLocalRing.FlatDescent.solution`: the statement of
  `IsRegularLocalRing.of_flat_of_isLocalHom`.

## Implementation notes

The source picks a single resolution of `κ` of length `d` and identifies its last syzygy. It is
shorter, and the same mathematics, to run the two syzygy comparisons as one induction on `d`:
`hasProjectiveDimensionLE_of_baseChange` proves, for every `n`, that a finite `R`-module `M` with
`pd_S(S ⊗_R M) ≤ n` has `pd_R M ≤ n`.

Both halves of the inductive step are one dimension shift,
`hasProjectiveDimensionLE_succ_iff_ker`: for a surjection `p : P → M` from a projective module,
`pd M ≤ n + 1` if and only if `pd (ker p) ≤ n`. This is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.ShortExact.hasProjectiveDimensionLT_X₃_iff` read off the presentation,
and it is the form in which the source quotes Lemma 00O5. The step chooses a finite free
presentation `0 → ker p → R^k → M → 0`, shifts along it over `R`, and shifts along its base change
`0 → ker q → S^k → N → 0` over `S`; that the base change of the syzygy is the syzygy of the base
change is exactly flatness, in the form of `LinearMap.tensorKerEquiv`. The base case `n = 0` is
Lemma 00O1 (`projective_iff_baseChange`), which is the only place flatness and locality of the
homomorphism are used together.

Universes. `R : Type u` and `S : Type v` are independent, so `S ⊗[R] M` lands in
`Type (max u v)` while Proposition 00O7 bounds the projective dimension of the objects of
`ModuleCat.{v} S` only. The induction therefore carries an `S`-linear equivalence
`S ⊗[R] M ≃ₗ[S] N` with `N : Type v` rather than `ModuleCat.of S (S ⊗[R] M)` itself. In the
inductive step that equivalence is transported to the syzygies by `kerLinearEquivOfLadder`, which
identifies the kernels of the two rows of a commuting square whose columns are equivalences; at the
start of the proof it comes from a surjection `S^k → S ⊗[R] κ`, which models the finite `S`-module
`S ⊗[R] κ` in `S`'s own universe as a quotient of `S^k`.

## References

* [StacksProject 00OF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OF)
-/

namespace Stacks.RegularLocalRing.FlatDescent

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing
open scoped TensorProduct



/-- **Dimension shift along a presentation.** If `p : P → M` is a surjection of `A`-modules with
`P` projective, then `M` has projective dimension at most `n + 1` exactly when its syzygy `ker p`
has projective dimension at most `n`. This is Lemma 00O5 in the form the source uses it. -/
private lemma hasProjectiveDimensionLE_succ_iff_ker {A : Type u} [Ring A] {P M : Type u}
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module A P] [Module.Projective A P] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
    {p : P →ₗ[A] M} (hp : Function.Surjective p) (n : ℕ) :
    HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of A M) (n + 1) ↔
      HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of A (LinearMap.ker p)) n := by
  have hcomp : p.comp (LinearMap.ker p).subtype = 0 := by ext x; exact x.2
  have hSE : (ShortComplex.moduleCatMk (LinearMap.ker p).subtype p hcomp).ShortExact :=
    { exact := by
        rw [ShortComplex.moduleCat_exact_iff_range_eq_ker]
        exact (LinearMap.exact_iff.mp p.exact_subtype_ker_map).symm
      mono_f := by rw [ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective]; exact (LinearMap.ker p).injective_subtype
      epi_g := by rw [ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective]; exact hp }
  exact hSE.hasProjectiveDimensionLT_X₃_iff n ((IsProjective.iff_projective _).mp inferInstance)

/-- The two rows of a commuting square whose columns are linear equivalences have isomorphic
kernels: if `q ∘ₗ e₂ = e₃ ∘ₗ g` with `e₂` and `e₃` equivalences, then `ker g ≃ₗ ker q`. -/
private noncomputable def kerLinearEquivOfLadder {A : Type*} [Ring A] {X₂ X₃ Y₂ Y₃ : Type*}
    [AddCommGroup X₂] [AddCommGroup X₃] [AddCommGroup Y₂] [AddCommGroup Y₃]
    [Module A X₂] [Module A X₃] [Module A Y₂] [Module A Y₃]
    {g : X₂ →ₗ[A] X₃} {q : Y₂ →ₗ[A] Y₃} (e₂ : X₂ ≃ₗ[A] Y₂) (e₃ : X₃ ≃ₗ[A] Y₃)
    (h : q ∘ₗ (e₂ : X₂ →ₗ[A] Y₂) = (e₃ : X₃ →ₗ[A] Y₃) ∘ₗ g) :
    LinearMap.ker g ≃ₗ[A] LinearMap.ker q :=
  (e₂.submoduleMap (LinearMap.ker g)).trans (LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (by
    have h₂ : Submodule.comap (e₂ : X₂ →ₗ[A] Y₂) (LinearMap.ker q) = LinearMap.ker g := by
      rw [← LinearMap.ker_comp, h, LinearMap.ker_comp, e₃.ker, Submodule.comap_bot]
    rw [← h₂, Submodule.map_comap_eq_of_surjective e₂.surjective]))

/-- **Descent of a bound on the projective dimension along a flat local homomorphism.** If `M` is
a finite `R`-module whose base change to `S` has projective dimension at most `n`, then `M` itself
has projective dimension at most `n`. The base change is presented through an `S`-linear
equivalence with a module `N` in the universe of `S`, so that the hypothesis can be supplied by a
global dimension bound for `ModuleCat.{v} S`. -/
@[ega "IV 6.2.1" "(ii)"]
private theorem hasProjectiveDimensionLE_of_baseChange (R : Type u) (S : Type v) [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalRing S]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] [Module.Flat R S] :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
      (N : Type v) [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N], ((S ⊗[R] M) ≃ₗ[S] N) →
      HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of S N) n →
        HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of R M) n := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro M _ _ _ N _ _ e hN
    rw [← projective_iff_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_zero] at hN ⊢
    have hSN : Module.Projective S N := (IsProjective.iff_projective N).mpr hN
    exact (IsProjective.iff_projective M).mp
      (projective_iff_baseChange.mpr (Module.Projective.of_equiv' e.symm))
  | succ n ih =>
    intro M _ _ _ N _ _ e hN
    -- a finite free presentation `0 → ker p → R^k → M → 0` of `M`
    obtain ⟨k, p, hp⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin' R M
    -- its base change `0 → ker q → S^k → N → 0`, moved into the universe of `S`
    let ε : (S ⊗[R] (Fin k → R)) ≃ₗ[S] (Fin k → S) :=
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.basis (M := (Fin k → R)) S (Pi.basisFun R (Fin k))).equivFun
    let q : (Fin k → S) →ₗ[S] N :=
      e.toLinearMap ∘ₗ TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor S S p ∘ₗ ε.symm.toLinearMap
    have hq : Function.Surjective q :=
      (e.surjective.comp (LinearMap.baseChange_surjective S hp)).comp ε.symm.surjective
    -- flatness: the base change of the syzygy is the syzygy of the base change
    have eK : (S ⊗[R] LinearMap.ker p) ≃ₗ[S] LinearMap.ker q :=
      (LinearMap.tensorKerEquiv S S p).trans (kerLinearEquivOfLadder ε e (by ext x; simp [q]))
    exact (hasProjectiveDimensionLE_succ_iff_ker hp n).mpr
      (ih _ _ eK ((hasProjectiveDimensionLE_succ_iff_ker hq n).mp hN))

/-- If `R → S` is a flat local homomorphism of local rings with `R` Noetherian and `S` regular,
then `R` is a regular local ring. -/
@[ega "0 17.3.3", ega "IV 6.5.1"]
public theorem solution {R : Type u} (S : Type v) [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [Algebra R S] [Module.Flat R S]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)] [IsRegularLocalRing S] : IsRegularLocalRing R := by
  -- `dim S` is the natural number `d`, and `S` has global dimension at most `d` (Proposition 00O7)
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ : ∃ d : ℕ, ringKrullDim S ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    ⟨_, le_of_eq (IsRegularLocalRing.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal (R := S)).symm⟩
  have hgd : ∀ N : ModuleCat.{v} S, HasProjectiveDimensionLE N d :=
    (IsRegularLocalRing.exists_leftResolution_free_finite_and_hasProjectiveDimensionLE hd).2
  -- a model of `S ⊗_R κ` in the universe of `S`, as a quotient of some `S^k`
  obtain ⟨k, f, hf⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin' S (S ⊗[R] ResidueField R)
  -- the residue field of `R` has projective dimension at most `d`
  have hκ : HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of R (ResidueField R)) d :=
    hasProjectiveDimensionLE_of_baseChange R S d (ResidueField R) _
      (f.quotKerEquivOfSurjective hf).symm (hgd _)
  -- Serre's criterion (Proposition 00OC)
  exact ((isRegularLocalRing_tfae (R := R)).out 1 3).mp
    ((projectiveDimension_ne_top_iff _).mpr ⟨d, hκ⟩)

end Stacks.RegularLocalRing.FlatDescent

/-!
# Regularity descends along a flat local homomorphism

Let `R → S` be a local homomorphism of local Noetherian rings which is flat, and assume `S` is
regular. Then `R` is regular.

The source's proof. Let `𝔪 ⊂ R` be the maximal ideal, `κ = R/𝔪` the residue field and `d = dim S`.
Choose a resolution `F_• → κ` by finite free `R`-modules and put `K_d = Ker(F_{d-1} → F_{d-2})`.
Flatness of `R → S` keeps `0 → K_d ⊗_R S → F_{d-1} ⊗_R S → … → F_0 ⊗_R S → κ ⊗_R S → 0` exact, and
the global dimension of `S` is `d` (Proposition 00O7), so `K_d ⊗_R S` is a finite free `S`-module
(Lemma 00O5). By Lemma 00O1 — a finite module over `R` is finite projective as soon as its base
change to `S` is, for a flat local homomorphism — `K_d` is a finite free `R`-module. Hence `κ` has
finite projective dimension over `R`, and `R` is regular by Proposition 00OC.

## Main results

* `IsRegularLocalRing.of_flat_of_isLocalHom`: a local Noetherian ring admitting a flat local
  homomorphism to a regular local ring is itself regular.

## Implementation notes

"Regular" for a local Noetherian ring is Mathlib's `IsRegularLocalRing` (Definition 00KU), a class
extending `IsLocalRing` and `IsNoetherianRing`; so the source's three hypotheses on `S` — local,
Noetherian, regular — are the single instance `[IsRegularLocalRing S]`, and the two on `R` that the
conclusion does not itself provide in usable form are spelled out as `[IsLocalRing R]` and
`[IsNoetherianRing R]`.

The homomorphism is `algebraMap R S` for an `[Algebra R S]`, Mathlib's way of naming a ring map;
flatness is `Module.Flat R S`, which is what `RingHom.Flat (algebraMap R S)` unfolds to, and "local
homomorphism" is `IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)`. That hypothesis pair is the one of the sibling
`Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_flat_of_isLocalHom`, whose name this one mutates; by that lemma the map
is automatically faithfully flat, so `[Module.FaithfullyFlat R S]` would be an equivalent
hypothesis here, but flat plus local is the source's wording and the shape a caller can supply
directly.

`[IsLocalRing R]` is redundant — `RingHom.domain_isLocalRing` derives it from `IsLocalRing S`,
`IsLocalHom (algebraMap R S)` and `Nontrivial R`, the latter being
`(algebraMap R S).domain_nontrivial`. It is kept because the source's hypothesis is a local
homomorphism *of local rings*: for a non-local `R` the class `IsLocalHom` says only that units pull
back to units, which is the same condition solely by that derivation, and the Mathlib sibling keeps
both localities for the same reason. `[IsNoetherianRing R]` is redundant in the mathematics too,
Noetherianness descending along the faithfully flat `R → S`, but Mathlib has no such descent lemma,
the source assumes it, and its proof uses it twice: to resolve `κ` by finite free modules and to
apply Proposition 00OC.

`S` is an explicit argument, occurring in neither the conclusion nor any other explicit argument;
for the same reason this is not an instance, `R` having no way to know a flat local extension of
itself. The two rings live in independent universes.

Only the local statement of the source is given. The variant for a flat ring map with regular
target follows from it by localizing `S` at a prime lying over `𝔪` and using that a localization of
a regular ring is regular (Lemma 0AFS), and belongs to the tag that states it.

Faithfulness. (1) No hypothesis is dead: flatness is essential — `k[x]/(x²) → k` is a local
surjection onto a regular local ring and the source is not regular — and so is locality of the
homomorphism, since for `R = (k[x, y]/(xy))_{(x, y)}` the localization `S = R_{(x)}` is a field,
flat over `R`, while `R` is not regular; `IsLocalRing R` and `IsNoetherianRing R` are both entailed
by the conclusion `IsRegularLocalRing R`, so neither decorates a special case. (2) The scalars and
base are the source's: flatness is that of `S` as an `R`-module, along `algebraMap R S` and no
localization of it, and both regularity assertions are about the rings `R` and `S` themselves. (3)
The map the source names is pinned: the hypotheses are about `algebraMap R S`, not about the
existence of some flat local homomorphism `R → S`. (4) The instantiation is not degenerate: the map
`k[x]_{(x)} → k[x, y]_{(x, y)}` satisfies every hypothesis, the target being free hence flat over
the polynomial ring and the localization flat over that, and it is regular of dimension `2` over a
source regular of dimension `1`, both rings nontrivial.

